{
  "blake2fPrecompileAcrossUpgrades": {
    "_info": {
      "comment": "The BLAKE2 compression precompile across the schedule, and the control for the other three. It arrives at PHOENIX rather than Atlantis, which is what makes it useful beyond its own coverage: its gas falls by about 25,000 at Atlantis exactly as the others do, while its output stays empty for two more upgrades. That separates EIP-161's change to the cost of touching a non-existent account from a precompile actually appearing -- two things that coincide in every other precompile here and would otherwise be indistinguishable. Its cost is one gas per round and the probe requests one round, so the arrival shows as a single gas unit on top of the call. The probe copies its calldata into memory, calls the address, and keeps the first output word plus the gas the call consumed. Slot 1 is an unconditional liveness marker. A FIXED gas amount is forwarded rather than GAS: before Gas Reprice, asking a call for more gas than remains is an out-of-gas error rather than being clamped, so GAS as the argument kills the probe at the two earliest upgrades and reads as the precompile being absent everywhere. READ THE GAS COLUMN AS TWO SEPARATE CHANGES. The fall of about 25,000 at Atlantis is EIP-161 ceasing to charge for touching a non-existent account on a zero-value call; it is NOT the precompile appearing, and the blake2f fixture beside this one proves that by showing the same fall at Atlantis while its output stays empty until Phoenix.",
      "oracle": "core-geth production, evm t8n at each upgrade's rules, chain id 61",
      "oracle-version": "v1.12.21-unstable",
      "generated": "2026-08-23",
      "signing": "txbytes carries the signed transaction; the signing key is a filling input, not a fixture field, and the harness reads `sender`.",
      "slots": "0 = first word of the call's output buffer, zero when nothing was written. 1 = liveness marker. 2 = gas the call consumed.",
      "address": "0x09",
      "eips": "EIP-152 at Phoenix",
      "role": "control for the Atlantis gas fall in the other three",
      "unfilled-no-fork-name": "No expectation for ETC_Thanos: the generator's fork table has no name for them, so their rules cannot be selected. A tooling gap, not a claim that the case does not apply.",
      "unfilled-not-a-state-rule": "No expectation for ETC_DAOFork, ETC_DAOWars, ETC_FrontierThawing, ETC_MESSOff, ETC_MESSOn: these change no state-transition rule, so a state fixture has nothing to assert about them. Covering them needs block-level or chain-selection tests."
    },
